<%#
  The one list on the site that was not an `Entry`. It rendered its own row —
  14px at weight 400, date first, no ruby bar, colour-only hover — against the
  19px/600 rows the same reader had just scanned on `/posts/`, so the last list
  on a post taught a different language from every list that led them there.
  It is an `Entry` now: same title size, same edge-note date, same field and
  ruby bar on hover.

  The label is the section head, in `PageSection`'s words and at its `md`
  remove from the list. A labelled section does not also need a rule drawn
  over it, and the one that was here made a third hairline in the footer.
%>

<nav aria-label="Related posts">
  <%= render Stack.new(space: :md) do %>
    <h2 class="m-0 text-label text-mauve-11">Related</h2>

    <%= render Stack.new(space: :xxs) do %>
      <% posts.each do |post| %>
        <%= render PostRow.new(
          post: post,
          show_reading: false,
          show_tags: false,
          clamp_title: true,
        ) %>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
</nav>
